  "worked_solution": "Since $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{AB},$ the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is twice the length of the segment $\\overset{―}{AM}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2AM & =AB \\\\ 2(3x-2) & =4x+6 \\\\ 6x-4 & =4x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we subtract $4x$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-4-4x & =4x+6-4x \\\\ 2x-4 & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we add $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-4+4 & =6+4 \\\\ 2x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{2} & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
